INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<p>Cropping <strong>Coriander</strong> As one of the most popular medicinal and aromatic plants, it requires precise planning across all stages of production. However, no stage is as critical as <strong>planting</strong> because if the quantity of coriander seed per hectare is not calculated accurately, all efforts in irrigation and farm management will be in vain. Many farmers still use traditional methods and scatter seed blindly, whereas with proper knowledge of planting density and irrigation systems, they can achieve twice the yield. In this comprehensive guide, we not only discuss numbers but also explain how to adjust <strong>the quantity of coriander seed per hectare</strong> based on climatic conditions, soil type, and irrigation methods (drip and tape) to ensure optimal efficiency for your field.</p><h2>Why is precise calculation of coriander seed per hectare important?</h2><p>The seeding mix you use directly impacts plant competition for water and nutrients. If planting density is too high, plants grow thin and weak, becoming more susceptible to fungal diseases. Conversely, low density fails to maximize the land\'s production potential and allows weeds to establish. Dill is a crop with rapid initial growth; therefore, from an economic perspective, using excess seed increases costs and creates unfavorable moisture conditions at the soil surface. [link:appropriate seed quantity per hectare to improve yield](https://navar-abyari.ir/miqdori-tukhmi-musir-dar-gektar-rohayi-afzoyishi-hosil/)</p><h2>Impact of tape drip irrigation systems on spacing selection</h2><p>One of the greatest achievements in modern agriculture is the ability to precisely control root zone moisture using <strong>tape drip</strong> . In drip irrigation systems, planting distance must align with the diameter and discharge rate of the drip emitters. When using tape drip, the distance between planting rows (longitudinal spacing) and the distance between tubes (transverse spacing) are determined. Dill is typically planted at distances of 5 to 15 centimeters along the row. [link:tape drip irrigation installation method](https://navar-abyari.ir/type-irrigation-tape-installation-method/)</p><p></p><p>The key point is that when using tape drip, plant density under the irrigation shadows should be such that roots reach adjacent roots to prevent water evaporation. Therefore, calculating <strong>dill seed amount per hectare</strong> must be based on these standard distances. The greater the distance between tape drip tubes, the more the longitudinal planting spacing can be slightly increased to ensure better coverage.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-گشنیز-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="مقدار بذر گشنیز در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>Seed rate per hectare for coriander</figcaption></figure><h2>Standard seed amount for coriander per hectare</h2><p>For precise calculation, we must consider three main variables: row length, row spacing, and the weight required per square meter. Generally, the coriander seed rate per hectare can range from 15 kg to 25 kg depending on climatic conditions. However, to achieve optimal quality, we recommend the following standard average:</p><table><caption>Coriander seed calculation guide table</caption><tbody><tr><th>Row spacing (cm)</th><th>Spacing along the row (cm)</th><th>Number of plants per hectare</th><th>Approximate seed amount (kg)</th></tr><tr><td>30</td><td>5</td><td>6,666</td><td>Approximately 15 to 17</td></tr><tr><td>25</td><td>4</td><td>10,000</td><td>Approximately 20 to 23</td></tr><tr><td>20</td><td>3</td><td>16,666</td><td>Approximately 25 to 28</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Note that these figures are based on a seed weight of 300 grams per square meter (assuming appropriate planting density). If your seeds are hilleted (peas), you must definitely consider a lower amount to prevent initial root clumping. [link:measure of harvest in one hectare full guide](https://navar-abyari.ir/mikyori-hosili-marza-dar-yek-gektar-rahnamoi-purra/)</p><h2></h2><p>Coriander seeds, due to their very small size, are always a planting challenge. Because of the small seed size, during broadcasting, excessive accumulation in one spot and gaps in another can occur. To solve this problem, roller planting methods can be used, which are very effective for coriander.</p><h2>Practical tips for planting coriander with tape</h2><p>In the tape irrigation system, you can benefit from planting flexibility. To get the best result, please pay attention to these practical points:</p><ol><li><strong>Soil Preparation:</strong> Before installing the drip line, disc the soil to a depth of 30-40 cm to ensure cilantro roots grow without resistance. Cilantro requires loose soil.</li><li><strong>Drip Line Spacing:</strong> Ensure the drip tape is positioned approximately 15 to 20 cm from the center of the planting row so that roots are adequately within the wetted zone.</li><li><strong>Pressure Management:</strong> The appropriate pressure for drip tape is generally 1 to 1.5 bar. For cilantro, which has sensitive roots, lower pressure (100-120) is preferred to prevent root asphyxiation.</li><li><strong>Weed Management:</strong> Since the row spacing for cilantro is narrow, using mulching (chipping) is highly effective.</li></ol><p></p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-گشنیز-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="مقدار بذر گشنیز در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>Crop cilantro seed rate per hectare</figcaption></figure><h2>Local technical and climatic notes</h2><p>If you are in a high-humidity area, reduce planting density to minimize fungal disease. In dry regions, humidity is lower, but cilantro requires more frequent irrigation. [link: al ray bil akhadid](https://navar-abyari.ir/al-ray-bil-akhadid/) is an older irrigation method that consumes more water compared to tape drip. For cilantro, a crop highly sensitive to moisture, tape drip is the more reliable method. Using tape drip helps maintain stable root zone moisture even in hot weather, which increases oil yield in cilantro.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions about cilantro seed rate per hectare</h2><h3>1. Does the cilantro seed rate per hectare differ between winter and summer planting?</h3><p>Yes. In summer planting, when temperatures are higher, you can use a slightly higher density than the average to reduce heat and drought stress on the plants. In winter planting, if your region is cold, a lower density is generally recommended.</p><h3>2. Can cilantro seed be planted directly on the tape drip?</h3><p>No, never place seed directly on the tape drip. You must sow the seed at a specific distance from the tape. The tape\'s function is to deliver water to the roots, not to hold the seed. Placing seed on the tape can cause growing plants to contact the tubing, which may damage the stems.</p><h3>3. What is the best stage for calculating seed rate accurately?</h3><p>First, test the seed viability (germination rate). If it is below 90%, increase the seed rate to achieve the target plant population.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-گشنیز-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="مقدار بذر گشنیز در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>Seed rate per hectare for cilantro (dill)</figcaption></figure><h3>4. How to adjust drip tape for planting cilantro?</h3><p>For cilantro, the row spacing is very narrow (approximately 20 to 30 cm). Drip tape with smaller diameters (e.g., 16 mm) and 20-25 cm emitters is more suitable. [link:Drip Tape Maintenance and Costs](https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%86%da%af%d8%b4%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b1%d9%8a-%d9%86%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%aa%db%8c%d9%84-%d9%88-%d9%87%d8%b2%d9%8a%d9%86%d9%87/)</p><h3>5. Does drip tape promote early growth in cilantro?</h3><p>Yes, because irrigation reaches the root zone at optimal temperatures, cilantro growth in drip tape systems is typically 10 to 15 days faster than with manual irrigation.</p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Selecting the correct dill seed rate per hectare is an art that combines agricultural knowledge with modern irrigation. By using drip line methods and adhering to planting density, you can deliver products with excellent quality and higher economic yield. Always remember that uniform seed distribution is the key to success. Our final recommendation is to use treated seeds for your next planting and start irrigation with a suitable low-pressure drip line. This approach not only optimizes water consumption but also enhances the quality of your dill for export markets.</p>\n<p><strong>Related articles:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/miqdori-tukhmi-musir-dar-gektar-rohayi-afzoyishi-hosil/">miqdori tukhmi musir dar gektar rohayi afzoyishi hosil</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/hosilnokiya-chukandari-qand-dar-gektar-omilhoi-muassisir/">hosilnokiya chukandari qand dar gektar omilhoi muassisir</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/type-irrigation-tape-installation-method/">type irrigation tape installation method</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%86%da%af%d9%87%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b1%db%8c-%d9%86%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%aa%db%8c%d9%be-%d9%88-%d9%87%d8%b2%db%8c%d9%86%d9%87/">Drip Line Maintenance and Costs</a></p>','Coriander Seed Rate per Hectare: A Comprehensive Guide for Maximum Productivity in Drip and Teflon Band Irrigation','In this comprehensive article, learn all the details of precise coriander seed rate calculation per hectare. From selecting the appropriate density for dripper line irrigation to key tips for increasing production. A practical guide for professional farmers.','publish','closed','closed','coriander-seed-rate-hectare-drip-teflon-irrigation-guide',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
INSERT INTO `ha_postmeta` (`post_id`,`meta_key`,`meta_value`) SELECT @translation_id,'_navar_translation_queue_key','article-translation:crop-335:en-US' WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_postmeta` WHERE post_id=@translation_id AND meta_key='_navar_translation_queue_key');
